    not_duplicate_of: []  # a955
    pr_ref:  # a955
    description: "WI-vubad validation on airflow (2026-04-11) showed the openapi-gen regex is applied correctly but ~10% of symbols from flagged-generated files still appear in the dead-code candidate list. Concrete residual: 57 candidates in /openapi-gen/ paths (down from 599 pre-fix), all from 4 file types — CancelablePromise.ts, request.ts, OpenAPI.ts, ApiError.ts — across 3 copies of the openapi-gen tree in airflow. Symbol names leaking through: path, process, append, headers, encodePair, getUrl, onCancel, onReject, onResolve, CancelablePromise.{then,catch,cancel,finally,constructor}, Interceptors.{constructor,eject,use}, ApiError.constructor, CancelError.constructor. The file-level is_generated flag IS flipping (90% of candidates correctly dropped), but something about how hypergumbo extracts and tier-classifies individual symbols from these 4 file types leaves a subset exposed. Likely cause: tier demotion cascades at file level but symbol records carry an earlier tier snapshot, or the TS analyzer extracts certain symbol shapes (arrow functions, class method exports) via a code path that bypasses the file-level metadata. Investigate in js_ts.py symbol extraction and supply_chain.py tier propagation. Low priority because bulk effect (90% drop) already delivered; this is the residual long tail."  # a955
    fields: {}  # a955
